Official checkpoint artifacts
-----------------------------

Tiny / paper checkpoint:
  Repository: https://huggingface.co/piddnad/ddcolor_paper_tiny
  Revision: cf9fd99c1d7472689ec7413441c1b799a51866a3
  File: pytorch_model.bin
  Bytes: 220372845
  SHA-256: 8a1277bc90a1bfbb6d2d83933a9a6bc821931879ca93e26e4fcec12165d41fce
  Card license: Apache-2.0

Large / ModelScope-quality checkpoint:
  Repository: https://huggingface.co/piddnad/ddcolor_modelscope
  Revision: 060f67494e31883a4b13cb27f889f3154847ada4
  File: pytorch_model.bin
  Bytes: 911914869
  SHA-256: d81711971ec59200da26d5e8a1afae8dd3778d495ea8ad7a7dadc769f403f7e7
  Card license: Apache-2.0

The official model zoo states that both checkpoints were trained on ImageNet;
the ConvNeXt initialization also carries ImageNet-22K lineage. ImageNet's
database access agreement restricts dataset use and redistribution:
https://image-net.org/accessagreement

The checkpoint publisher nevertheless gives each exact weight repository an
explicit Apache-2.0 artifact license. LibreYOLO records both facts. The model
weights are a maintainer-visible provenance decision, and no ImageNet image or
database file is bundled or downloaded by this family.

The official ``ddcolor_artistic`` checkpoint is deliberately excluded because
the upstream model zoo says it also uses undisclosed private data.

